  "Number": 8,
  "Question": "If \\(a = -2,\\) the largest number in the set\n\n\\[\\left\\{ -3a,\\ 4a,\\ \\dfrac{24}{a},\\ a^2,\\ 1 \\right\\}\\]\n\nis",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(-3a\\)",
    "B": "\\(4a\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\dfrac{24}{a}\\)",
    "D": "\\(a^2\\)",
    "E": "\\(1\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "Substitute \\(-2\\) for \\(a\\), using parentheses to keep its negative sign attached. Since \\(a=-2\\ne0\\), the quotient is defined. The values are\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n-3a&=-3(-2)=6,\\\\\n4a&=4(-2)=-8,\\\\\n\\frac{24}{a}&=\\frac{24}{-2}=-12,\\\\\na^2&=(-2)(-2)=4.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nThe fifth value is \\(1\\). The negative values are smaller than the positive ones, and \\(6>4>1\\). Thus the largest number is \\(-3a=6\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{A}\\).",
